  "description": "<p>This task is to resolve the issue of users who have acl:READ access on a resource not being able to perform a HEAD request.</p>\n\n<p>The issue can be reproduced as follows:<br/>\n1. Create a resource<br/>\ncurl -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -v -X PUT  <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/test\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/test</a><br/>\n2. Give 'testuser' READ access to the above resource<br/>\ncurl -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin -v -X PUT  <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/test/fcr:acl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/test/fcr:acl</a> --data-binary \"@acl.ttl\" -H \"Content-Type: text/turtle\"<br/>\n..where \"acl.ttl\" is:<br/>\n```<br/>\n@prefix acl: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#</a>&gt; .<br/>\n@prefix foaf: &lt;<a href=\"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/</a>&gt; .</p>\n\n<p>&lt;#restricted&gt; a acl:Authorization ;<br/>\n   acl:agent \"testuser\" ;<br/>\n   acl:mode acl:Read ;<br/>\n   acl:accessTo &lt;/rest/test&gt; .<br/>\n```<br/>\n3. Notice success on GET<br/>\ncurl -i -u testuser:testpass -X GET <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/test\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/test</a><br/>\n4. BOOM: Notice failure on HEAD<br/>\ncurl -i -u testuser:testpass -I <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/test\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/test</a></p>",
